	(text "RTC (RV-3032-C7, App. Manual Rev. 1.3)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "73da9a63-5847-5cce-ac5f-06795fe8f7f9"))
	(text "No backup bridge: VBACKUP tied to VSS through R9, BSM = 00 (factory default).\nA cell swap resets the time (set it again over NFC); the aging offset (EEPROM C1h)\nand the other configuration EEPROM survive.\nWhy: an MLCC bridge would need 36 uF (270 nA, 25 C) to 100 uF (750 nA, -40..85 C)\nto hold 60 s from 1.75 V down to VLOW 1.3 V. Its IR spec (50 MOhm.uF) is a 50 s\nself-discharge time constant at any size, so no MLCC can be guaranteed to bridge 60 s,\nand worst-case standby leakage would be 2-5.5 uA against a ~1 uA budget." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 124.46 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c6da77b5-367e-5cd1-8b5b-aaac66fcae93"))
	(text "I2C pull-ups 10k: idle-high bus draws nothing; 0.3 mA per line only while a line is low.\nRise time 10k x ~30 pF = 0.25 us (meets 400 kHz). Run the bus at 100 kHz when VBAT < 2.0 V\n(RV-3032 needs VDD >= 2.0 V for 400 kHz).\nFirmware: set FD = 1 Hz or NCLKE = 1 in EEPROM C0h/C3h. The factory default is a 32.768 kHz\nCLKOUT, which costs ~1 uA into 10 pF." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 147.32 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2d93c176-3f6b-52eb-90c4-b65ec1226b24"))
	(label "VBAT" (at 124.46 76.2 90) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "77752795-8bfd-5890-bb96-961b35d5e4e4"))
